 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Acyclicity of injectives on $\\mathbf P^1_s$",
 "statement": "For an injective sheaf $I$ of $\\mathbf F_\\ell$-modules on\n$X=\\mathbf P^1_A$, the restriction\n$I_0$ is $\\Gamma(X_0,-)$-acyclic: $H^q(X_0,I_0)=0$ for all $q>0$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-p1/lemma-weil-pbc-p1-injective-acyclic.md",
  "place": "node lemma-weil-pbc-p1-injective-acyclic, order 1141",
  "external": [
   {
    "document": "Stacks Project",
    "place": "Tag 0A5H"
   }
  ]
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The affine-cover lemma gives vanishing for $q>1$ because $\\mathbf P^1$ is\ncovered by two affines. For $q=1$, apply the representation lemma. For each\nfinite summand, finite-direct-image exactness and Leray identify its $H^1$ on\n$X_0$ with $H^1((V_i)_0,\\underline{M_i})$. Torsor comparison lifts every\ncomponent to $H^1(V_i,\\underline{M_i})$, and Leray returns a class in\n$H^1(X,(h_i)_*\\underline{M_i})$. Their finite sum maps to zero in $H^1(X,I)$\nbecause $I$ is injective. Restriction of the commuting square shows that the\noriginal class is zero. The source locator is Tag `0A5H`.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
